        "id": 264773,
        "name": "",
        "username": "LonelyMan",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/l/f4b2a3/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2026-01-08T22:27:40.566Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I would argue that sixty to eighty percent of episodes qualify as “dumb time things” just because they talk about what month a made up comic wasn’t actually published.</p>\n<p>About the Oblivion infinity stuff: I don’t think any chain reaction that starts with a finite number of destructions can “get rolling” enough to ever be infinite.  However I also don’t believe that the multiverse is infinite, or rather there are two multiverses, a finite one which OblivAeon is destroying, and an infinite one which is all Sentinels games ever.  I like to think of this as the 5th and 6th dimensions of time; just as there’s a finite amount of 4D time since the universe began, there’s also a finite number of split timelines in 5D, but there’s an effectively if not literally infinite number of 6D versions of each of those 5D timelines.  (This also neatly addresses the sandwich bag; there is a 5D loaf of bread split into finite slices, one of which was bagged, and there are an infinite number of different RPG campaigns in that one slice of bread.)  All of the timelines in the canon multiverse are 5D, and there are a specific number of them, because the same forces that gave rise to the singular entities also constructed the multiverse, with its single Inversiverse and Xtremiverse and Magic Freedom Fiveiverse, instead of infinite ones of each, its single Ur-Space, and its single copy of each singular entity (plus OblivAeon, minus Wager Master post bagging).</p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"TakeWalker\" data-post=\"2\" data-topic=\"29342\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/takewalker/48/5677_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> TakeWalker:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Drinking food and eating beverages sounds like exactly the kind of catering you’d get at an avant-garde art show.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>So, Soylent and boba tea?</p>",
        "post_number": 6,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2026-01-09T00:56:19.378Z",
